#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2552
msgid "Max Fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2553
msgid "Max fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2558
msgid "This setting represents the maximum speed of your fan."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2567
msgid "Max"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2572
msgid ""
"This is the highest printable layer height for this extruder, used to cap "
"the variable layer height and support layer height. Maximum recommended "
"layer height is 75% of the extrusion width to achieve reasonable inter-layer "
"adhesion. If set to 0, layer height is limited to 75% of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2583
msgid "Max print speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2588
msgid ""
"When setting other speed settings to 0 Slic3r will autocalculate the optimal "
"speed in order to keep constant extruder pressure. This experimental setting "
"is used to set the highest print speed you want to allow."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2603
msgid ""
"This experimental setting is used to set the maximum volumetric speed your "
"extruder supports."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2613
msgid "Max volumetric slope positive"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2618
msgid ""
"This experimental setting is used to limit the speed of change in extrusion "
"rate for a transition from lower speed to higher speed. A value of 1.8 mm³/"
"s² ensures, that a change from the extrusion rate of 1.8 mm³/s (0.45 mm "
"extrusion width, 0.2 mm extrusion height, feedrate 20 mm/s) to 5.4 mm³/s "
"(feedrate 60 mm/s) will take at least 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2623
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2641
msgid "mm³/s²"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2631
msgid "Max volumetric slope negative"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2636
msgid ""
"This experimental setting is used to limit the speed of change in extrusion "
"rate for a transition from higher speed to lower speed. A value of 1.8 mm³/"
"s² ensures, that a change from the extrusion rate of 5.4 mm³/s (0.45 mm "
"extrusion width, 0.2 mm extrusion height, feedrate 60 mm/s) to 1.8 mm³/s "
"(feedrate 20 mm/s) will take at least 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2647
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2648
msgid "Min fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2653
msgid "This setting represents the minimum PWM your fan needs to work."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2662
msgid "Min"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2667
msgid ""
"This is the lowest printable layer height for this extruder and limits the "
"resolution for variable layer height. Typical values are between 0.05 mm and "
"0.1 mm."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2675
msgid "Min print speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2680
msgid "Slic3r will not scale speed down below this speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2687
msgid "Minimal filament extrusion length"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2692
msgid ""
"Generate no less than the number of skirt loops required to consume the "
"specified amount of filament on the bottom layer. For multi-extruder "
"machines, this minimum applies to each extruder."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2701
msgid "Configuration notes"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2705
msgid ""
"You can put here your personal notes. This text will be added to the G-code "
"header comments."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2716
msgid "Only retract when crossing perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2721
msgid ""
"Disables retraction when the travel path does not exceed the upper layer's "
"perimeters (and thus any ooze will be probably invisible)."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2727
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:4524
msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: Enable ooze prevention
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2732
msgid ""
"This option will drop the temperature of the inactive extruders to prevent "
"oozing."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2738
msgid "Detect bridging perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2743
msgid ""
"Experimental option to adjust flow for overhangs (bridge flow will be used), "
"to apply bridge speed to them and enable fan."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2749
msgid "Filament parking position"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2753
msgid ""
"Distance of the extruder tip from the position where the filament is parked "
"when unloaded. This should match the value in printer firmware."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2761
msgid "Extra loading distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2765
msgid ""
"When set to zero, the distance the filament is moved from parking position "
"during load is exactly the same as it was moved back during unload. When "
"positive, it is loaded further,  if negative, the loading move is shorter "
"than unloading."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2773
msgid "Purging volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2777
msgid ""
"Determines purging volume on the wipe tower. This can be modified in "
"Filament Settings ('filament_purge_multiplier') or overridden using project-"
"specific settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2785
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2823
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2841
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2855
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigDef.cpp:114
msgid "Perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2790
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for perimeters. Set zero to "
"disable acceleration control for perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2802
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for external perimeters. Set "
"zero to use the value for perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2810
msgid "Perimeter extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2815
msgid ""
"The extruder to use when printing perimeters and brim. First extruder is 1."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2828
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for perimeters. "
"You may want to use thinner extrudates to get more accurate surfaces. If "
"left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x "
"nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for example 200%) "
"it will be computed over nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2846
msgid ""
"Speed for perimeters (contours, aka vertical shells). Set to zero for auto."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2859
msgid ""
"This option sets the number of perimeters to generate for each layer. Note "
"that Slic3r may increase this number automatically when it detects sloping "
"surfaces which benefit from a higher number of perimeters if the Extra "
"Perimeters option is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2863
msgid "(minimum)"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2871
msgid "Post-processing scripts"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2876
msgid ""
"If you want to process the output G-code through custom scripts, just list "
"their absolute paths here. Separate multiple scripts with a semicolon. "
"Scripts will be passed the absolute path to the G-code file as the first "
"argument, and they can access the Slic3r config settings by reading "
"environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2888
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2910
msgid "Pressure advance"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2894
msgid ""
"Controls how the pressure advance value is emitted into g-code for this "
"filament. 'Disabled' does not emit any pressure advance command, leaving the "
"printer to use the pressure advance value set in the filament's start g-code "
"(or the firmware default). 'Enabled' emits the configured pressure advance "
"value. 'Automatic Calibration' emits the configured pressure advance value "
"and then triggers the firmware's automatic pressure advance calibration."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2905
msgid "Automatic Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2916
msgid ""
"Pressure Advance (also called Linear Advance in some firmware) compensates "
"for nozzle pressure to achieve sharper corners. Proper value helps reduce "
"bulging on deceleration and under-extrusion on acceleration."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2926
msgid "Printer vendor"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2929
msgid "Name of the printer vendor."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2951
msgid "Raft contact Z distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2956
msgid ""
"The vertical distance between object and raft. Ignored for soluble interface."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2965
msgid "Raft expansion"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2970
msgid "Expansion of the raft in XY plane for better stability."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2979
#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3887
msgid "First layer density"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2984
msgid "Density of the first raft layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2992
msgid "Raft first layer expansion"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:2999
msgid "Expansion of the raft first layer to improve adhesion to print bed."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3007
msgid "Raft layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3012
msgid ""
"The object will be raised by this number of layers, and support material "
"will be generated under it."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3020
msgid "Slice resolution"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3025
msgid ""
"Minimum detail resolution, used to simplify the input file for speeding up "
"the slicing job and reducing memory usage. High-resolution models often "
"carry more detail than printers can render. Set to zero to disable any "
"simplification and use full resolution from input."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3037
msgid "G-code resolution"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3042
msgid ""
"Maximum deviation of exported G-code paths from their full resolution "
"counterparts. Very high resolution G-code requires huge amount of RAM to "
"slice and preview, also a 3D printer may stutter not being able to process a "
"high resolution G-code in a timely manner. On the other hand, a low "
"resolution G-code will produce a low poly effect and because the G-code "
"reduction is performed at each layer independently, visible artifacts may be "
"produced."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3054
msgid "Minimum travel after retraction"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3059
msgid ""
"Retraction is not triggered when travel moves are shorter than this length."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3066
msgid "Retract amount before wipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3071
msgid ""
"With bowden extruders, it may be wise to do some amount of quick retract "
"before doing the wipe movement."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3079
msgid "Retract on layer change"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3084
msgid "This flag enforces a retraction whenever a Z move is done."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3090
msgid "Retraction length"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3095
msgid "Retraction Length"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3096
msgid ""
"When retraction is triggered, filament is pulled back by the specified "
"amount (the length is measured on raw filament, before it enters the "
"extruder)."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3104
#: src/slic3r-shared/src/Slic3r/App/Plater/MeasureDialog.cpp:152
msgid "Length"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3108
msgid "Retraction Length (Toolchange)"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3109
msgid ""
"When retraction is triggered before changing tool, filament is pulled back "
"by the specified amount (the length is measured on raw filament, before it "
"enters the extruder)."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3118
msgid "Ramping slope angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3123
msgid "Slope of the ramp in the initial phase of the travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3132
msgid "Use ramping lift"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3137
msgid ""
"Generates a ramping lift instead of lifting the extruder directly upwards. "
"The travel is split into two phases: the ramp and the standard horizontal "
"travel. This option helps reduce stringing."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3145
msgid "Maximum ramping lift"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3150
msgid ""
"Maximum lift height of the ramping lift. It may not be reached if the next "
"position is close to the old one."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3160
msgid "Steeper ramp before obstacles"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3165
msgid ""
"If enabled, PrusaSlicer detects obstacles along the travel path and makes "
"the slope steeper in case an obstacle might be hit during the initial phase "
"of the travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3172
msgid "Lift height"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3177
msgid "Lift height applied before travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3186
msgid "Only lift Above Z"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3192
msgid "Only lift Z above"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3193
msgid ""
"If you set this to a positive value, Z lift will only take place above the "
"specified absolute Z. You can tune this setting for skipping lift on the "
"first layers."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3201
msgid "Only lift Below Z"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3207
msgid "Only lift Z below"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3208
msgid ""
"If you set this to a positive value, Z lift will only take place below the "
"specified absolute Z. You can tune this setting for limiting lift to the "
"first layers."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3217
msgid "Deretraction extra length"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3222
msgid ""
"When the retraction is compensated after the travel move, the extruder will "
"push this additional amount of filament. This setting is rarely needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3230
msgid "Extra length on restart"
msgstr ""

#: src/slic3r-domain/src/Slic3r/Domain/ConfigBoxesFDM.cpp:3234
msgid ""
"When the retraction is compensated after changing tool, the extruder will "
"push this additional amount of filament."
msgstr ""

